:"not significant","donor_padj":0.999342,"donor_log2fc":0.0290169,"donor_lfcse":0.0848806,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":4.22044e-06},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"RYK","gene_symbol_current":"RYK","gene_id":"ENSG00000163785","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"higher in AD","nucleus_padj":6.0934e-06,"nucleus_log2fc":0.119429,"nucleus_score":4.67822,"pct_ad":0.347844,"pct_control":0.337192,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.822612,"donor_log2fc":0.115333,"donor_lfcse":0.101434,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.0118597}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"Ex","gene_id":"ENSG00000163785","module":"blue","kme":0.32378,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.391996,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_id":"ENSG00000163785","module":"blue","kme":0.1324,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.842971,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000163785","entrez_id":["6259"],"uniprot":["P34925"],"ncbi_summary":"The protein encoded by this gene is an atypical member of the family of growth factor receptor protein tyrosine kinases, differing from other members at a number of conserved residues in the activation and nucleotide binding domains. This gene product belongs to a subfamily whose members do not appear to be regulated by phosphorylation in the activation segment. It has been suggested that mediation of biological activity by recruitment of a signaling-competent auxiliary protein may occur through an as yet uncharacterized mechanism. The encoded protein has a leucine-rich extracellular domain with a WIF-type Wnt binding region, a single transmembrane domain, and an intracellular tyrosine kinase domain. This protein is involved in stimulating Wnt signaling pathways such as the regulation of axon pathfinding. Alternative splicing results in multiple transcript variants encoding distinct isoforms. [provided by RefSeq, Feb 2012].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"P34925","text":"May be a coreceptor along with FZD8 of Wnt proteins, such as WNT1, WNT3, WNT3A and WNT5A. Involved in neuron differentiation, axon guidance, corpus callosum establishment and neurite outgrowth. In response to WNT3 stimulation, receptor C-terminal cleavage occurs in its transmembrane region and allows the C-terminal intracellular product to translocate from the cytoplasm to the nucleus where it plays a crucial role in neuronal development."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}